    ("What is 'Self-Regulation' (Self-Management) in emotional intelligence?", "The ability to control or redirect disruptive emotions and impulses, and adapt flexibly to changing realities", ["Repressing all human emotions until an explosive outburst occurs", "Ignoring all feedback from colleagues and superiors", "Forcing subordinates to obey orders through fear"], "Self-regulation enables emotional composure under crisis, ethical consistency, and measured responses rather than knee-jerk reactions."),
    ("What is 'Empathy' in leadership?", "The ability to understand and share the feelings, perspectives, and emotional needs of others", ["Agreeing with every complaint voiced by team members", "Crying whenever someone in the office feels unhappy", "Giving cash bonuses to every employee unconditionally"], "Empathy allows leaders to understand unstated concerns, mentor effectively, and build high-trust, collaborative environments."),
