    ("What is 'Democratic Leadership' (Participative Style)?", "A style where the leader encourages team participation and consensus-building in decision-making", ["A style where no leader exists and everyone does whatever they want", "A style where only the youngest employee makes all decisions", "A style where decisions are made strictly by senior government decree"], "Participative leadership fosters employee buy-in, creative problem-solving, and engagement, though decision-making may take longer."),
    ("What is 'Laissez-Faire Leadership' (Delegative Style)?", "A hands-off style where the leader provides minimal direction and allows team members complete autonomy", ["A micromanagement style where every email is proofread by the boss", "A style based on military drill commands and daily physical inspections", "A leadership approach focused exclusively on firing underperformers"], "Laissez-faire leadership works well with highly skilled, self-motivated experts, but risks drift and confusion with inexperienced teams."),
