    ("What is 'Transactional Leadership' primarily characterized by?", "A leadership approach based on an exchange relationship of contingent rewards and corrective penalties (management by exception)", ["Leading purely through moral virtue, humility, and self-sacrifice", "Completely ignoring whether employees meet their deadlines", "Focusing on lifelong spiritual transformation of followers"], "Transactional leaders focus on contractual clarity, performance standards, reward compliance, and corrective interventions."),
    ("Who coined the term and conceptual framework of 'Servant Leadership' in 1970?", "Robert K. Greenleaf", ["Peter Drucker", "Jack Welch", "Niccolò Machiavelli"], "Greenleaf proposed that great leaders focus first on serving the needs of employees, customers, and community."),
    ("In Stephen Covey's 'The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People', what is Habit 1?", "'Be Proactive' (taking responsibility and initiative rather than reacting passively to circumstances)", ["'Begin with the End in Mind'", "'Put First Things First'", "'Think Win-Win'"], "Being proactive emphasizes expanding one's Circle of Influence rather than complaining about one's Circle of Concern."),
    ("In Stephen Covey's framework, what does Habit 2: 'Begin with the End in Mind' advise?", "Envisioning your ultimate destination, values, and core principles before starting any endeavor", ["Leaving work early at the end of every business day", "Postponing all difficult planning tasks until project conclusion", "Focusing exclusively on immediate short-term financial gains"], "Beginning with the end in mind ensures that the ladder you are climbing is leaning against the right wall."),
